    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nHooke & MacDonald are delighted to present No. 58 Shrewsbury Square, a superior quality two bedroom apartment positioned within one of Dublin 4's most renowned and carefully managed residential developments.\n\nShrewsbury Square comprises 80 apartments across three multi storey blocks, set above a secure basement car park and landscaped podium gardens that create a quiet and private setting throughout the scheme. A seven day concierge service further enhances the quality of day to day management for residents.\n\nNo. 58 offers a well designed and generously proportioned interior. The entrance hall features an attractive tiled floor, recessed lighting and a useful storage cupboard. This leads into a spacious open-plan kitchen, living and dining room. The kitchen reflects the high quality specification of the development, fitted with high gloss wall and floor units and integrated appliances including a gas hob with extractor fan, oven, microwave, coffee machine, fridge freezer and dishwasher, all set against tiled flooring with recessed lighting. The living/dining area is carpeted, also with recessed lighting, and opens directly to a sunny southwest facing balcony overlooking the landscaped communal gardens.\n\nThe main bedroom is a superb, spacious double room with built-in wardrobes, recessed lighting and direct access to the balcony. It includes a luxurious ensuite bathroom fitted with a bath, wc, washand basin with mirrored overhead storage press, heated towel rail, recessed lighting and fully tiled walls and floors. Bedroom two is also a generous double with built-in wardrobes, recessed lighting and balcony access. A well appointed shower room completes the accommodation, featuring a double shower cubicle, wc, washand basin with mirrored storage press, recessed lighting and fully tiled walls and floor. The apartment benefits from a designated underground car parking space and secure basement storage in keeping with the wider development layout.\n\nSituated along Sandymount Avenue, residents enjoy immediate proximity to Sandymount DART Station, offering swift access to the city centre and coastal transport routes. The area sits between the InterContinental Hotel and the villages of Ballsbridge and Sandymount, providing a wide choice of cafés, restaurants, local shops and everyday amenities. It is also within comfortable walking distance of the RDS, Herbert Park, and the Aviva Stadium. Despite this high level of convenience, the development remains notably peaceful, with its elevated podium layout and landscaped grounds contributing to a calm, private and secure residential environment.\n\nNo. 58 Shrewsbury Square presents an excellent opportunity to acquire a high quality apartment in a well managed and ideally positioned Dublin 4 development. With its south west facing balcony, secure parking, strong management, concierge service and outstanding access to transport, sports venues and neighbourhood amenities, it offers a comfortable and appealing home in one of the city's most convenient residential settings. \n\nViewings are strictly by appointment only."
      },
